<title>ITALY: Fiat Punto top selling European car in Jan.</title>
<headline>Fiat Punto top selling European car in Jan.</headline>
<dateline>TURIN 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fiat's Punto subcompact was Europe's top-selling model in January, ahead of the Volkswagen Golf and the Astra, produced by GM's Opel unit, industrial sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>The sources said the Punto sold around 56,000 units.</p>
<p>Fiat Auto grabbed an overall 13 percent share of the European market in January, behind the Volkswagen group with more than 16 percent but ahead of Opel with a 12.7 percent share, the sources said.</p>
<p>--Milan newsroom +392-66102321</p>
</text>
